WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:13.260
[Narrator:] This young man, John, has returned
to his doctor for a checkup

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:16.680
because a premarital blood test was reported
positive.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:19.040
Dr. Johnson now inquires into John's history.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:25.760
Thereafter, he proceeds to a thorough physical
examination,

00:00:25.769 --> 00:00:30.560
which he records completely on a permanent record form.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:34.540
He takes a specimen of blood for a second
serologic test and instructs John

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:37.620
to return later for the report.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:44.320
[Dr. Johnson:] So, this positive blood test
confirms the first one we took.

00:00:44.329 --> 00:00:47.640
There's no doubt in my mind now, John, that you have syphilis.

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:51.980
[John:] Well, doctor, what...

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:54.920
[Dr. Johnson:] It means that we will begin
treatment right away.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:57.250
It will take a year and a half at least.

00:00:57.250 --> 00:01:01.930
[John:] A year and a half, it's--that's a
long time.

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:05.960
But if you think you can cure me, I guess
it's worth it.

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:11.720
[Dr. Johnson:] Now John, the important thing
is that you must take your treatments regularly

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:13.380
every week.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:21.360
You see, if we don't find syphilis soon enough,
or the treatment isn't regular or long enough,

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:23.850
serious conditions often result.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:29.520
But in your case, if you stick to it and come
in for every treatment,

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:32.189
there's not much doubt that we can make you
well.

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:37.140
[John:] Well, the trouble is doctor, I haven't
very much money.

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:42.439
[Dr. Johnson:] Well, you see, the health department
provides me with drugs at no charge.

00:01:42.439 --> 00:01:46.049
I think we can arrange things so you can afford
your treatments.

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:51.439
[John:] That's swell, Dr. Johnson, and I sure
want to stick with you.

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:55.400
[Dr. Johnson:] Now, there's another thing
that you should know, John.

00:01:55.409 --> 00:01:59.380
You can give your disease to other people.

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:04.760
So it's very important that you shouldn't
have sexual relations or kiss anyone

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:07.480
until I say it's all right.

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:12.700
Unfortunately, this means that you can't
be married as soon as you had planned.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:15.040
It wouldn't be fair to your girl.

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:19.790
[John:] Well, will I ever be able to be married,
doctor?

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:22.459
[Dr. Johnson:] Oh yes, of course, John.

00:02:22.459 --> 00:02:25.640
Only you must wait until I tell you it's all
right.

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:29.970
Now, you should see that your fiancee has
an examination.

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:32.959
You will take care of that, won't you?

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:36.580
[John:] Yeah. I guess that's the square thing
to do, doctor.

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:38.780
[Dr. Johnson:] Of course, it is John.

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:43.340
Now John, I want you to tell me where you
think you picked up this disease.

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:48.200
You should tell me all about it because whoever
gave it to you, can give it to others,

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:51.180
and she should receive the same attention
you are getting.

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:53.380
Of course, your name won't be used.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:59.440
[John:] Well, it was about a year ago. I don't
know who she was.

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:02.280
Her name was Sally I think.

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:06.390
[Dr. Johnson:] Sally. Hmm. Do you remember
her address?

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:13.060
[John:] Ah, Third Street, next to the store
on the corner of Cypress.

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:14.530
[Dr. Johnson:] Third.

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:19.180
[Narrator:] Every case of venereal disease
should be reported to the health officer.

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:24.420
The report should include information about
contacts.

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:30.740
Once the case is diagnosed, the doctor's attention
is focused upon the plan of treatment.

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:35.489
This table shows the arsenical drugs which
are best to use in various types of syphilitic infection.

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:42.379
and the arsenical drugs which should not be used in certain types.

00:03:42.379 --> 00:03:45.549
For early acquired syphilis, the arsenical
drugs of choice

00:03:45.549 --> 00:03:50.870
are arsphenamine, neoarsphenamine, and arsenoxide.

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:55.799
Bismuth has largely replaced mercury, particularly in the treatment of early syphilis.

00:03:55.799 --> 00:03:58.409
Of the many bismuth compounds which are available,

00:03:58.409 --> 00:04:04.629
perhaps the most frequently used is a suspension
of bismuth subsalicylate in oil.

00:04:04.629 --> 00:04:11.980
The iodides are of little or no value in the
treatment of early syphilis.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:18.410
The dosages given in this recommended scheme
of treatment for early syphilis are for arsphenamine.

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:23.790
The recommended dose is higher for neoarsphenamine
and lower for arsenoxide.

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:26.960
Treatment for early syphilis should start
with an arsenical drug

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:30.430
in order to control infectiousness quickly.

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:36.760
Regularity is extremely important, particularly
during the first six months of treatment.

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:43.240
Arsenicals are alternated with bismuth in
order to avoid the development of drug resistance.

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:48.660
The first course of bismuth should be short,
consisting of about four doses,

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:53.490
subsequently increasing to six, eight, and
10 doses.

00:04:53.490 --> 00:05:00.240
A minimum of 30 injections of an arsenical and
40 injections of bismuth should be given.

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:06.180
This makes a total of 18 months of treatment
for cases of early syphilis.

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:09.180
After this eighteen months, the patient may
be placed on probation

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:13.389
if physical examination, blood test, spinal
fluid examination,

00:05:13.389 --> 00:05:18.470
and x-ray examination of the heart and aorta are negative.

00:05:18.470 --> 00:05:24.410
The probationary period should extend for
at least one year after treatment is stopped.

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:26.370
During this time, blood tests should be made

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:33.800
and the skin and mucus membranes inspected
at intervals of from one to three months.

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:39.020
In a case of early syphilis, if the blood tests remain positive after six or eight months of treatment,

00:05:39.139 --> 00:05:44.299
perform a complete physical examination and examine the spinal fluid.

00:05:45.419 --> 00:05:48.779
The most frequent cause of sero-resistance in early syphilis

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:51.340
is involvement of the central nervous system.

00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:55.720
Therefore, in early syphilis, failure of the
blood test to show response to treatment

00:05:55.720 --> 00:05:58.000
should cause apprehension.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:03.860
In late syphilis, either acquired or congenital, sero-resistance in itself is not important.

00:06:06.389 --> 00:06:11.910
The gravity method of administrating arsenicals
is most frequently used for old arsphenamine.

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:16.430
This drug should never be used except under
rigidly controlled conditions,

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:21.070
since the danger of improper neutralization
is otherwise great.

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:31.750
The syringe technique is usually used for
other arsenical drugs.

00:06:32.140 --> 00:06:38.160
Neoarsphenamine should be injected slowly
and arsenoxide should be injected rapidly.

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:41.340
Bismuth and mercury should be injected very deeply

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:43.940
into the upper outer quadrant of the buttock,

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:47.940
so that the drug is deposited under the deepest
layer of muscle.

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:52.530
The barrel of the syringe should be pulled
back before the drug is injected

00:06:52.530 --> 00:06:56.419
to make sure that the needle is not in a blood
vessel.

00:06:56.419 --> 00:06:59.719
The physician should study the anatomic position
of the sciatic nerves

00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:02.080
so that he can avoid striking it.

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:08.380
Before administering antisyphilitic treatment, a physician should make himself

00:07:08.380 --> 00:07:10.380
thoroughly familiar with the reactions

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:15.319
which may occur and the danger signals which
call for discontinuance of the treatment

00:07:15.319 --> 00:07:18.039
or change in the type of treatment.

00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:23.080
Question each patient in regard to reactions
to the previous injection.

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:26.160
Inspect the skin at each visit for toxic dermatosis

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:30.760
such as this erythema or this purpura.

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:38.940
Inspect the sclera for jaundice.

00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:42.280
Look for early signs of exfoliated dermatitis,

00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:46.140
which is one of the most frequent serious reactions to arsenicals.

00:07:46.639 --> 00:07:50.479
An important danger signal is itching.

00:07:50.480 --> 00:08:00.440
Bismuth may cause pigmentation of the gums, ulceration of the tongue, or pigmented papules.

00:08:00.979 --> 00:08:05.509
In the management of late latent syphilis,
one should perform a physical examination,

00:08:05.509 --> 00:08:07.500
a spinal fluid examination,

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:11.420
and an x-ray examination of the heart before treatment is started

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:13.880
or as soon thereafter as possible.

00:08:14.420 --> 00:08:18.940
During the first year, give arsenicals and
bismuth in alternating courses

00:08:18.940 --> 00:08:21.660
of eight to 12 doses each.

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:26.080
During the second year, give about three 12-dose
courses of bismuth.

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:31.520
In this presentation, no attempt can be made to provide a detailed portrayal

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:34.180
of the treatment of late syphilis.

00:08:34.589 --> 00:08:38.300
In general, treatment should be guided by the fact that radical cure

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:42.440
can no longer be accomplished as in early
syphilis.

00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:47.500
The best that can be hoped for is the alleviation
of symptoms, healing of lesions,

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:53.660
restoration and maintenance of health, and
prevention of further progression or relapse.

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:59.940
Neurosyphilis, however, presents certain special
problems in therapy.

00:08:59.950 --> 00:09:05.589
So-called Wasserman fastness is not an indication
for the use of tryparsamide.

00:09:05.589 --> 00:09:09.610
This drug is useful only in neurosyphilis.

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:16.010
Trivalent arsenicals should always be chosen
when the central nervous system is not involved.

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:19.450
Before using tryparsamide, look for power
of the optic discs

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:22.090
and measure the visual fields carefully.

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:28.120
Optic atrophy in any degree is a contraindication to the use of tryparsamide,

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:32.640
since sudden blindness may result if this
condition is present.

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:36.519
Before each injection of tryparsamide, question
the patient

00:09:36.519 --> 00:09:41.980
in regard to symptoms such as shimmering vision
following the last injection.

00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:46.420
If such history is given, repeat the visual
field examination.

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:50.980
Contraction of the visual fields calls for
immediate discontinuance of the drug.

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:56.600
Malaria is induced in neurosyphilitic patients
by transfer of blood from a malaria patient.

00:09:56.600 --> 00:09:59.340
The non-tertian or quartan malaria is used.

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:05.220
Malaria therapy is used in severe or resistant
cases of asymptomatic neurosyphilis

00:10:05.220 --> 00:10:10.540
and in clinical neurosyphilis such as paresis, tabes, and optic atrophy.

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:17.640
Fever therapy should not be used in the treatment
of neurorecurrence in early syphilis

00:10:17.640 --> 00:10:22.420
unless intensified routine therapy fails to
eradicate the condition.

00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:28.520
Artificial fever therapy induced by mechanical
means is also widely used

00:10:28.529 --> 00:10:30.389
in the treatment of neurosyphilis.

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:33.880
Specially-trained personnel must be used in
this method,

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:39.780
but under properly controlled conditions,
it is as safe and effective as malaria therapy.

00:10:41.670 --> 00:10:46.040
Swift-Ellis Treatment is a highly technical
procedure which should be used only by an expert.

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:52.680
It is useful in optic atrophy and in the treatment of lightning pains and gastric crises of tabes dorsalis.

00:10:53.720 --> 00:11:00.860
Now, having reviewed the highlights of modern antisyphilitic therapy, let us return to Dr. Johnson.

00:11:02.310 --> 00:11:06.220
The case report which he makes to the health department is of  practical value to him

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:12.300
in the management of his patient, and results often in the referral to him of new patients.

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:17.360
Further interviews after a satisfactory doctor-patient relationship has been established

00:11:17.500 --> 00:11:20.060
may reveal additional contacts.

00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:24.459
These contacts should of course be reported
also.

00:11:24.459 --> 00:11:29.980
Let us see what happens now that Dr. Johnson
has sent his report to the health officer.

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:34.459
It will be incorporated into the health department
morbidity records.

00:11:34.459 --> 00:11:36.800
It also becomes a credit, so to speak,

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:43.209
against which the doctor may obtain drugs
supplied by the state health department.

00:11:43.209 --> 00:11:47.750
On the contact portion of the report, the
doctor has noted an alleged contact

00:11:47.750 --> 00:11:53.269
whom he would like the health department to
investigate by a home visit.

00:11:53.269 --> 00:11:57.589
The health officer turns the information over
to a followup worker.

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:04.930
She visits the alleged contact, explaining
that the health department has information

00:12:04.930 --> 00:12:08.700
that the person may have been exposed to a communicable disease,

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:12.200
and should see the doctor for an examination.

00:12:13.139 --> 00:12:15.440
The doctor examines the alleged contact

00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:20.420
and sends a specimen of blood to the health
department laboratory.

00:12:25.630 --> 00:12:32.230
The specimen, identified by a number, is carefully
handled by trained technicians.

00:12:44.080 --> 00:12:48.660
Usually, two or more tests are run on each
specimen.

00:12:55.050 --> 00:13:02.279
The laboratory reports to the doctor in non-ambiguous terms, positive, doubtful, or negative.

00:13:02.279 --> 00:13:03.720
This specimen is positive.

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:10.079
[Dr. Johnson:] Your report is positive. It
rather looks as though you have syphilis.

00:13:10.079 --> 00:13:13.779
If this report is confirmed by a checkup,
you will have to begin treatment.

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:16.580
[Sally:] But doctor, I have no money.

00:13:17.280 --> 00:13:21.840
[Dr. Johnson:] I understand. I think the best
thing for me to do is

00:13:21.840 --> 00:13:24.580
to send you to Dr. Ramsey at the health department.

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:28.570
You can get good treatment there at no cost.

00:13:29.440 --> 00:13:32.140
[Narrator:] Here is the clinic to which Sally
has been sent.

00:13:32.149 --> 00:13:34.350
This is the waiting room.

00:13:34.350 --> 00:13:40.029
To encourage patients to return to it week
after week, it should be orderly and cheerful.

00:13:40.029 --> 00:13:44.440
Here for example, colorful, educational posters
brighten the walls.

00:13:44.440 --> 00:13:47.290
There is always someone around to answer questions.

00:13:47.290 --> 00:13:52.079
In fact, time spent here by the patients [can?]
and will be utilized to good advantage

00:13:52.079 --> 00:13:57.540
by informal educational discussions and by
motion pictures.

00:13:57.540 --> 00:14:01.860
Evening hours are arranged for the convenience
of working patients.

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:05.889
Privacy and quiet are provided for the physical
examinations.

00:14:05.889 --> 00:14:09.629
Booths with a full complement of treatment equipment make possible rapid

00:14:09.629 --> 00:14:12.940
yet considered arsenical therapy.

00:14:12.940 --> 00:14:18.060
A separate room for bismuth injections contributes
convenience and comfort.

00:14:18.060 --> 00:14:22.620
Spinal punctures can also be given here.

00:14:26.399 --> 00:14:32.430
A clinic this large would have equipment for
darkfield examinations and gonorrhea smears.

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:35.630
The patient's first impression of a clinic
may be the last,

00:14:35.630 --> 00:14:41.209
unless he is made to feel at ease and aware
of the clinic's real interest in the case.

00:14:41.209 --> 00:14:46.120
Therefore, introduction to clinic routine
is made by a specially-trained worker chosen

00:14:46.120 --> 00:14:50.220
for her pleasing personality as well as educational
qualifications.

00:14:52.389 --> 00:14:57.220
The social worker's interview with the patient
is part of an extensive educational program

00:14:57.220 --> 00:14:59.820
carried on by the health department.

00:14:59.820 --> 00:15:02.740
This includes distribution of folders and
pamphlets telling the public

00:15:02.740 --> 00:15:06.640
about syphilis and gonorrhea and what to do about them.

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:12.110
It includes programs over radio stations.

00:15:12.110 --> 00:15:17.470
It includes posters in public places urging
people to see their doctors for blood tests.

00:15:20.300 --> 00:15:27.500
It includes movies before all kinds of organizations
and in theaters.

00:15:27.500 --> 00:15:32.180
And it includes talks and lectures before
many kinds of audiences.

00:15:34.480 --> 00:15:39.449
For example, here is the health officer telling a group of men the facts about syphilis and gonorrhea.

00:15:40.089 --> 00:15:44.769
He is giving them practical information about prophylaxis.

00:15:47.509 --> 00:15:51.430
When the physician is called upon to give
instruction in regard to prophylaxis,

00:15:51.430 --> 00:15:57.070
he should warn his patients that the only
sure prophylaxis is abstinence from sexual promiscuity.

00:16:00.649 --> 00:16:04.680
When specific instruction is indicated, however, a condom should be advised,

00:16:04.680 --> 00:16:09.780
since this method imposes a mechanical barrier against the transference of the infective agent.

00:16:10.880 --> 00:16:15.079
Patients should be advised against the purchase
of condoms of inferior quality.

00:16:16.760 --> 00:16:20.740
The use of the condom should be supplemented
by thorough washing of the genitalia

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:28.290
and adjacent parts with soap and water for
five minutes as soon as possible after exposure.

00:16:28.290 --> 00:16:32.529
Care should be taken to include the undersurface of the prepuce and the scrotum,

00:16:32.529 --> 00:16:36.910
the inner surfaces of the thighs, and the lower portion of the abdomen.

00:16:36.910 --> 00:16:41.769
A brush should not be used since this causes abrasions of the skin

00:16:41.769 --> 00:16:44.639
through which the infective agent may enter.

00:16:44.639 --> 00:16:47.519
After washing, the patient should urinate.

00:16:51.220 --> 00:16:55.220
Six cubic centimeters of two percent strong
silver protein solution

00:16:55.220 --> 00:17:01.080
is next injected into the urethra and the
patient holds it there for five minutes.

00:17:06.289 --> 00:17:10.339
The protargol solution should be freshly prepared.

00:17:10.339 --> 00:17:14.559
The last step of the procedure is to rub 33
percent calomel ointment

00:17:14.560 --> 00:17:17.600
into the genitalia and adjacent parts.

00:17:22.420 --> 00:17:28.539
Prophylaxis in women is only occasionally
useful, chiefly in cases of rape.

00:17:28.539 --> 00:17:33.599
The anatomy of the region makes the procedure
more difficult than in the male.

00:17:33.880 --> 00:17:39.720
Antisyphilitic treatment should never be used
as a prophylactic measure following exposure.

00:17:39.980 --> 00:17:45.200
Treatment for syphilis is not justified unless
the diagnosis of a syphilitic infection

00:17:45.200 --> 00:17:49.600
has been established by clinical and laboratory
evidence.

00:17:52.740 --> 00:17:56.120
To keep abreast of current developments in
the diagnosis, treatment,

00:17:56.120 --> 00:17:59.220
and public health aspects of syphilis,

00:17:59.230 --> 00:18:01.830
read Venereal Disease Information,

00:18:01.830 --> 00:18:05.910
one of the medical journals published by the
United States Public Health Service.

00:18:07.800 --> 00:18:13.800
[Dr. Johnson:] We as private practitioners
have an indispensable function in this nation's

00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:17.760
program for the control of syphilis.

00:18:17.760 --> 00:18:22.940
We must recognize our responsibilities and
our obligations.

00:18:27.400 --> 00:18:31.150
Do you remember what Sir William Osler said?

00:18:31.150 --> 00:18:40.789
Listen, "I see an incredulous look on some
faces, and I hear the whispered comment

00:18:40.789 --> 00:18:42.630
--'tis heard often enough--

00:18:42.630 --> 00:18:48.490
'Where is all this syphilis? It does not come
my way.'

00:18:48.490 --> 00:18:51.860
Yes, it does.

00:18:51.860 --> 00:19:02.700
The syphilis we see but do not recognize everywhere
awaits diagnosis, so protean are its manifestations."

00:19:04.580 --> 00:20:04.060
[ Music ]

